        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-10-15T16:52:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I have gone over this a few times in my head today. What is your use case that does not work right now that you need to change the code?\n\nThe code on ToT still seems correct to me.\n\nTo answer Gwendal\u0027s early questions: if you want any host event delivered through MKBP to successfully send while the SoC is sleeping, you must either leave CONFIG_MKBP_EVENT_WAKEUP_MASK undefined or ensure that BIT(EC_MKBP_EVENT_HOST_EVENT) or BIT(EC_MKBP_EVENT_HOST_EVENT_64) is defined in your mask\n\n----\n\n@Heng-Ruey, the suggestion does not seem correct. if mkbp wants to skip the interrupt, then it should skip it\n\n\n---\n\nI do think this code could be cleaned up with a few more comments. Maybe we can consolidate the keyboard passthrue with the mkcp_event_wake_mask too",
      "parentUuid": "66379388_1ace9adc",
      "revId": "83b83109ea127f5de6e4635e519e7a67587a1cb5",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7b9eb0a2_0f93b6c0",
        "filename": "common/mkbp_event.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 207,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002686
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-10-16T02:02:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Our use case is to have CONFIG_MKBP_HOST_EVENT_WAKEUP_MASK and CONFIG_MKBP_EVENT_WAKEUP_MASK at the same time.\nCONFIG_MKBP_HOST_EVENT_WAKEUP_MASK is for power button and CONFIG_MKBP_EVENT_WAKEUP_MASK is for EC_MKBP_EVENT_SENSOR_FIFO event.\n\nIf we use original code, CONFIG_MKBP_EVENT_WAKEUP_MASK section will not be executed.\nHmm...Seems like the priority of skip_interrupt is higher than wake up device.",
      "parentUuid": "f1ebb535_f08d069e",
      "revId": "83b83109ea127f5de6e4635e519e7a67587a1cb5",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
